      "rows": [
        {
          "dimension": "Regulatory",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "MiCA approval and a New York BitLicense reduce headline risk in key markets, but multi-jurisdiction licensing creates ongoing compliance cost and fragmented operational rules that could slow feature rollout.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Centralization",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "MoonPay sits as a custodial chokepoint between fiat rails and on-chain assets; its open-source Open Wallet Standard and non-custodial virtual accounts are partial offsets but the core onramp flow remains centralized.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Liquidity",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "The $160M emergency raise triggered by Trump memecoin demand demonstrates that extreme onboarding spikes can temporarily exhaust liquidity buffers, requiring rapid external capital injections.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Counterparty / Partner concentration",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Revenue and growth are heavily dependent on a small set of high-profile integrations — Mastercard, PayPal, Ripple, Uniswap — such that any single partner exit would materially impair volume.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Market",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Onramp volumes are pro-cyclical with crypto sentiment; fee compression from zero-spread stablecoin offers and agent rails narrows margin even as headline transaction counts grow.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Smart-contract / Technical",
